+.B \-\-sort field
+Sort the search results by the given field. This option can be specified
+multiple times; sort keys are applied from left to right and later keys
+break ties from earlier keys. Sorting requires buffering all results before
+printing. Supported fields are \fBpath\fR, \fBname\fR, \fBextension\fR,
+\fBsize\fR, \fBmodified\fR, \fBcreated\fR, \fBaccessed\fR, \fBdepth\fR,
+\fBtype\fR, \fBname-length\fR, \fBpath-length\fR, and \fBrandom\fR.
+.TP
+.B \-\-reverse
+Reverse the final sorted output.
+.TP
+.B \-\-dirs-first
+Group directories before other entries.
+.TP
+.B \-\-files-first
+Group regular files before other entries.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-case-sensitive
+Compare text sort keys case-sensitively (default: case-insensitive).
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-missing-last
+Place entries with missing values at the end (default: missing values sort first).
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort-natural
+Use natural ordering for text-based sort keys: embedded runs of digits are
+compared numerically (e.g. \fBfile9\fR < \fBfile10\fR < \fBfile20\fR).
+.TP
+.BI "\-\-sort-seed " n
+Fix the seed used by \-\-sort random to an unsigned 64-bit integer,
+making the shuffle deterministic and reproducible.
+.TP
 .B \-\-show-errors
 Enable the display of filesystem errors for situations such as insufficient
 permissions or dead symlinks.
